    502   564   541 |   550   591   596  a leaked session of the owner role does not stop the drop: the forced drop end
    259   466   321 |  1197  1251  1208  the teardown removes what a crashed worker left: clones, a locked template, ev
    632   518   545 |   457   538   537  a database that cannot be dropped is reported by the teardown, by name and rea
# In the 'after' tree the runner started cleanup beside templates in all three runs (it orders files by size and by the
# durations it cached; the two trees have caches of their own). One test of cleanup, which builds two templates and a clone,
# then waits for the clone lock that templates.db.test.ts holds for about a second during its test 'a hook that leaves a
# session open' (1.1 s). With one worker that neighbour does not exist, and the file takes the same time (table 1).
